<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 6.5 pct in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 6.5 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 6.5 percent in the week to April 2 over the equivalent week a year ago, figures from the Bank of England showed. Last week the rise was 9.3 percent.(figures in rounded billions of stg) -</p>
<p>			    Latest week  Previous week  Year-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation  21.81	  21.60	     20.47</p>
<p> Bankers deposits	1.94	   2.23		1.73</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
